{
    "song_id": 725797,
    "title": "Lane Boy",
    "language": "en",
    "lyricists": "[50268]",
    "lyrics": [
        {
            "section_id": "section_0",
            "type": "chorus",
            "performer": "",
            "lines": [
                {
                    "n": "0",
                    "text": "They say, \"Stay in your lane, boy, lane, boy\"",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "1",
                    "text": "But we go where we want to",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "2",
                    "text": "They think this thing is a highway, highway",
                    "persona_id": "Blurryface"
                },
                {
                    "n": "3",
                    "text": "But will they be alive tomorrow?",
                    "persona_id": "Blurryface"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "section_id": "section_1",
            "type": "verse",
            "performer": "",
            "lines": [
                {
                    "n": "0",
                    "text": "They think this thing is a highway",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "1",
                    "text": "If it was our way, we'd have a tempo change every other time change",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "2",
                    "text": "'Cause our minds change on what we think is good",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "3",
                    "text": "I wasn't raised in the hood",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "4",
                    "text": "But I know a thing or two about pain and darkness",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "5",
                    "text": "If it wasn't for this music I don't know how I would have fought this",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "6",
                    "text": "Regardless, all these songs I'm hearin' are so heartless",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "7",
                    "text": "Don't trust a perfect person and don't trust a song that's flawless",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "8",
                    "text": "Honest, there's a few songs on this record that feel common",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "9",
                    "text": "I'm in constant confrontation with what I want and what is poppin'",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "10",
                    "text": "In the industry, it seems to me that singles on the radio are currency",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "11",
                    "text": "My creativity's only free when I'm playin' shows",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "section_id": "section_2",
            "type": "chorus",
            "performer": "",
            "lines": [
